{"name":"Arid Landscape","hex":"#dcd6c6","fetched":"2026-11-01","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very dry.","Describing a very dry climate. Typically defined as less than 25 cm or 10 inches of rainfall annually."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arid"},{"term":"landscape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A portion of land or territory as defined by its landform, its geographical (and architectural) features.","A portion of land which the eye can comprehend in a single view, including all the objects thus seen."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To create or maintain a landscape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landscape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aridity","blocks":[{"text":"Aridity is a condition of geographical regions characterized by low annual precipitation, increased temperatures, and limited water availability. These areas, which make up approximately 43% of total global available land area, tend to fall upon degraded soils, and their health and functioning are key necessities of regulating ecosystems’ atmospheric components."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg/330px-1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aridity","wikidata":"Q1330709"},{"title":"Landscape","blocks":[{"text":"A landscape is the visible features of an area of land, its landforms, and how they integrate with natural or human-made features, often considered in terms of their aesthetic appeal. A landscape includes the physical elements of geophysically defined landforms such as mountains, hills, water bodies such as rivers, lakes, ponds and the sea, living elements of land cover including indigenous vegetation, human elements including different forms of land use, buildings, and structures, and transitory elements such as lighting and weather conditions. Combining both their physical origins and the cultural overlay of human presence, often created over millennia, landscapes reflect a living synthesis of people and place that is vital to local and national identity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg/330px-Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landscape","wikidata":"Q107425"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg/500px-1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg/500px-1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arid regions of the Western United States as mapped in 1893","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1893_Arid_regions_of_the_western_united_states.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg/500px-Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg/1280px-Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg/500px-Cumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACumulus_Clouds_over_Yellow_Prairie2.jpg"}